var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-reference","page":"API reference","text":"Pages = [\"api.md\"]","title":"API reference"},{"category":"module","location":"api/#StreamingInference.StreamingInference","page":"API reference","text":"StreamingInference\n\nDomain-general layer of the pipeline: configuration and provenance, signal processing of sampled records, spectral features, the estimator interface between the conditioning chain and the method applied to each window, evaluation and decision thresholds, and the streamed consumption of a delivered record (run interface, coverage, window scheduling, causal whitening, replay, alert tables). Nothing in it depends on a physical domain or on a particular estimator.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.StreamingInference"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.ANIMATION_PX_PER_UNIT","page":"API reference","text":"ANIMATION_PX_PER_UNIT\n\nRaster scale of an animation in pixels per typographic point. A GIF is read on screen, so two pixels per point on the 900 pt canvas (1800 px wide) is its resolution, against four for the printed figures. Whole numbers only, see check_frame_scale.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.ANIMATION_PX_PER_UNIT"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.ANNOTATION_FONTSIZE","page":"API reference","text":"ANNOTATION_FONTSIZE\n\nType size [pt] of in-axis annotations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.ANNOTATION_FONTSIZE"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.CHANNEL_COMBINATIONS","page":"API reference","text":"CHANNEL_COMBINATIONS\n\nHow extract_features combines the synchronous channels of a window: :mean (features of the channel-averaged periodogram) or :max (the features of every channel, combined by the value farthest towards a signal).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.CHANNEL_COMBINATIONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.FEATURE_SETS","page":"API reference","text":"FEATURE_SETS\n\nThe feature sets of extract_features: :whitened (two band powers, entropy, log power spread), :paper (the raw-window moments of Isfan et al. 2025), and :bands (one power per band between consecutive band_edges, entropy, log power spread).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.FEATURE_SETS"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.FIGURE_COLORS","page":"API reference","text":"FIGURE_COLORS\n\nSemantic colours shared by every figure of the project (Okabe–Ito palette), each with a single use: data (scores, time series, measured points), label (labelled spans), threshold (the decision threshold, black, dashed in every figure), training and validation (the two blocks), noise and signal (score distributions, and the detected-event markers), fit (fitted or model curves), false_alarm (the false-alarm rate wherever it is drawn), target (a requested or reference rate: the far target, the 1 / stretch rule).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.FIGURE_COLORS"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.FIGURE_FONTSIZE","page":"API reference","text":"FIGURE_FONTSIZE\n\nType size [pt] of axis labels and legends.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.FIGURE_FONTSIZE"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.FIGURE_SIZE","page":"API reference","text":"FIGURE_SIZE\n\nCanvas of a single-panel figure in typographic points, (width, height): the base layout every figure scales from. Each further stacked main panel adds PANEL_HEIGHT, each auxiliary strip (a counter or residual panel) STRIP_HEIGHT; see figure_size.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.FIGURE_SIZE"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.FIGURE_STROKES","page":"API reference","text":"FIGURE_STROKES\n\nDarker same-hue counterparts of FIGURE_COLORS, under the same keys, for marker outlines and histogram bar edges.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.FIGURE_STROKES"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.LEGEND_STYLE","page":"API reference","text":"LEGEND_STYLE\n\nKeyword arguments of the horizontal legend placed above the axes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.LEGEND_STYLE"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.PANEL_HEIGHT","page":"API reference","text":"PANEL_HEIGHT\n\nHeight [pt] added to FIGURE_SIZE by each stacked main panel beyond the first.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.PANEL_HEIGHT"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.PIPELINE_ROOT","page":"API reference","text":"PIPELINE_ROOT\n\nThe pipeline root set for the current scope by with_pipeline_root; nothing outside any.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.PIPELINE_ROOT"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.STRIP_HEIGHT","page":"API reference","text":"STRIP_HEIGHT\n\nHeight [pt] added to FIGURE_SIZE by each auxiliary strip, a counter or residual panel beneath the main panels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.STRIP_HEIGHT"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.TICK_FONTSIZE","page":"API reference","text":"TICK_FONTSIZE\n\nType size [pt] of tick labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.TICK_FONTSIZE"},{"category":"constant","location":"api/#StreamingInference.TIMER","page":"API reference","text":"TIMER\n\nPackage-wide TimerOutput accumulating the wall time and allocations of every pipeline stage (@timeit TIMER \"stage\" ...); report_timing prints its table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.TIMER"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.AbstractTelemetryRun","page":"API reference","text":"AbstractTelemetryRun\n\nA producer run as seen by the consumer. An adapter implements run_geometry, list_batches, read_batch, arrival_events, and run_state; the consumer never writes into the run.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.AbstractTelemetryRun"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.AbstractWindowEstimator","page":"API reference","text":"AbstractWindowEstimator\n\nA method applied to one conditioned window of a time series (a detector score, a parameter estimate, a posterior summary, a forecast). The chain around it — delivery, gaps, window scheduling, conditioning, calibration, evaluation — does not depend on the method. Concrete estimators declare their memory with estimator_memory.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.AbstractWindowEstimator"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.AbstractWindowScorer","page":"API reference","text":"AbstractWindowScorer <: AbstractWindowEstimator\n\nAn estimator whose output is one scalar score per window, larger meaning more evidence for the event class, bounded by score_bounds. The detection chain (threshold, persistence, crediting) acts on it. A scorer implements window_score.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.AbstractWindowScorer"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.ArrivalEvent","page":"API reference","text":"ArrivalEvent\n\nOne row of the producer's arrival feed: the mission sim_time, the batch name, the event (:ingested, :retry, :lost, :pruned, or :other for values unknown to this version), and the attempt counter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.ArrivalEvent"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.BatchRecord","page":"API reference","text":"BatchRecord\n\nOne telemetry batch as seen by the consumer: name (LIVE_batch_<k> or ARCH_batch_<k>), global 1-based index, live flag, rows covered in the payload, content_epoch of its first sample, and state (:ground, :lost, or :pruned).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.BatchRecord"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.Coverage","page":"API reference","text":"Coverage()\n\nSet of delivered payload rows as sorted, disjoint UnitRange{Int} intervals, updated by add! and remove!; the order of arrivals is irrelevant to the resulting set.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.Coverage"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.EstimatorMemory","page":"API reference","text":"EstimatorMemory\n\nMemory trait of an AbstractWindowEstimator: Stateless or Stateful.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.EstimatorMemory"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.FeatureMap","page":"API reference","text":"FeatureMap(; feature_set = :whitened, low_band = (1e-3, 5e-3),\n           high_band = (5e-3, 1e-1), band_edges = [1e-3, 5e-3, 1e-1],\n           combination = :mean)\n\nThe spectral features of a conditioned window (extract_features): the feature set and its analysis bands [Hz]. band_edges is validated (check_band_edges) for every set, as the conditioning of a run records it, and used only by the :bands set. combination says how the channels of a multichannel window enter (CHANNEL_COMBINATIONS) and has no effect on a single channel.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.FeatureMap"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.GapEvent","page":"API reference","text":"GapEvent(first_window, last_window, cause, declared_at)\n\nA run of consecutive windows first_window:last_window that a Stateful estimator will not see, declared at mission time declared_at before the first window after it is released. cause is :lost (the window's own rows, or more of its conditioning stretch than the coverage bound admits, fell in a lost or pruned batch), :undelivered (not delivered by the end of the record), or :horizon (not delivered within the order horizon while later windows were waiting).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.GapEvent"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.MemoryTelemetryRun","page":"API reference","text":"MemoryTelemetryRun(geometry, payload, events; lost = String[])\n\nIn-memory run used by the tests: the whole payload, an arrival feed events, and the names of batches declared lost. Batch k holds payload rows batch_rows(k, P); every batch of the payload exists. A matrix payload holds several synchronous channels, one per column.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.MemoryTelemetryRun"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.OrderedCommit","page":"API reference","text":"OrderedCommit(last_window; order_horizon = nothing, late_policy = :skip)\n\nRelease of the windows of a replay to a Stateful estimator in content order. A window is conditioned when it becomes evaluable, exactly as for a Stateless one, and held (PendingWindow); windows are released by strictly increasing index, each once, and a run of windows that can never be scored is declared by one GapEvent instead, which the estimator receives (estimator_gap!) before the window after it. last_window is the last window of the record, 0 when its length is unknown.\n\nA window can never be scored when its own rows, or more of its conditioning stretch than the coverage bound admits, fell in a lost or pruned batch (:lost). Without further bound a missing window holds back every later one until the end of the record, where the windows still missing are declared :undelivered. order_horizon, a time period, bounds that wait: when a later window has been held for longer than it, the windows missing before it are declared :horizon. A window that becomes evaluable after its gap was declared is late: skipped and counted (late_policy = :skip) or refused (:error).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.OrderedCommit"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.PendingWindow","page":"API reference","text":"PendingWindow\n\nA window conditioned when it became evaluable and held by an OrderedCommit until its release: its payload rows, the conditioned samples, complete_at and completing_batch, its coverage and psd_row (as in WindowRecord), and the wall time of its conditioning conditioning_ms, added to the scoring time at release so that inference_wall_ms means the same as for a stateless scorer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.PendingWindow"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.ReplayState","page":"API reference","text":"ReplayState(run, detector; min_coverage = 1.0, tdi_gap_dilation_sec = 0.0,\n            trailing_psd = nothing, order_horizon = nothing, late_policy = :skip)\n\nConsumer state of a replay: the batches of the run, the Coverage of delivered rows, the WindowScheduler, the delivered payload per batch, the scored windows, the number of arrival events consumed, under trailing_psd::TrailingWelch the current causal PSD estimate with the last delivered row it was made on, and, when the detector's scorer is Stateful, the OrderedCommit that releases its windows in content order (order_horizon, late_policy); the scorer is reset (reset_estimator!) on construction. Fed one event at a time by process_event! and closed by finalize_replay!.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.ReplayState"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.RunGeometry","page":"API reference","text":"RunGeometry\n\nSampling and batching geometry of a telemetry run: sample_rate [Hz], segment_duration_sec, batch_size (segments per batch), points_per_batch, the mission epoch start_sim_time, the producer's package_version, and payload_rows, the number of rows of the external payload the producer ingested (0 when unknown); the producer zero-pads its stream beyond the payload, and windows past that bound are not scored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.RunGeometry"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.ScheduledRecordRun","page":"API reference","text":"ScheduledRecordRun(schedule, record; check = true)\n\nThe delivery of one run applied to the content of a local record: batches, arrival events, geometry and state are those of schedule (an AbstractTelemetryRun), and every delivered batch is served from the rows it holds of record, a vector or a matrix with one column per channel. A producer that carries one payload column thus supplies the arrival process of a multichannel replay: the delivery of a batch is taken to be common to the synchronous channels of its rows.\n\nWith check, every batch served is compared with the batch the schedule itself delivers: the first column of record must hold those samples, value for value in single precision, or the record is not the content the run carried and the batch is refused. Rows beyond the record are zeros, as the producer pads its payload.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.ScheduledRecordRun"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.Stateful","page":"API reference","text":"Stateful()\n\nAn estimator that carries state from window to window (a reservoir, a sequential posterior) and so must see the windows in content order, each once, with every hole declared.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.Stateful"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.Stateless","page":"API reference","text":"Stateless()\n\nAn estimator whose output for a window depends on that window alone, so windows may be evaluated in any order, as they complete.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.Stateless"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.StreamingDetector","page":"API reference","text":"StreamingDetector(scorer, threshold; sample_rate, window_size, step_size,\n                  psd = nothing, highpass_cutoff_hz = 5e-4, highpass_order = 8,\n                  context_windows = 4)\n\nScoring of complete windows out of a partially delivered record with the same conditioning as the batch pipeline. A window is cut from the delivered stretch around it — up to context_windows window lengths on each side — which is high-passed and, when psd is given, whitened as a whole (condition_window); the conditioned window is scored by scorer (window_score) and alarms at threshold. Isolated windows without context are scored on their own samples (edge-affected, as the first windows of any record). The conditioning belongs to the detector, the method to the scorer, so any AbstractWindowScorer runs through the same replay.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.StreamingDetector"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.TrailingWelch","page":"API reference","text":"TrailingWelch(span_rows, refresh_rows, segment_length; edge_rows = 0, smoothing_dex = 0)\n\nCausal whitening of a replay. Each window is whitened by the median Welch estimate (welch_psd, segments of segment_length samples) of the delivered record behind it: every delivered run inside the last span_rows rows before the end of the window's conditioning stretch, each run high-passed as the detector high-passes every stretch — the order in which the batch pre-processor estimates its \"welch\" PSD — and the segments of all runs pooled, so that no segment spans a delivery hole. The high-pass rings at both ends of a run (the ends of the record in the batch pipeline, whose edge windows are dropped), so edge_rows rows are trimmed from each end of a high-passed run before it is segmented, and a run must hold a segment beyond that trim. A positive smoothing_dex smooths the estimate in log-frequency (smooth_psd), as [preprocessing] psd_smoothing_dex smooths the batch estimate the model's features were whitened with. Nothing that has not reached the ground enters the estimate, unlike a PSD of the whole record, which at every window of a streamed mission contains data still to be delivered. The estimate is redone once the end of that record has moved by refresh_rows rows since the previous one. While no delivered run behind a window holds a segment — at the start of a mission — the window is whitened by the previous estimate, and by the detector's own static PSD only before any estimate exists. A run of several channels gets one estimate per channel, each from that channel of the same delivered runs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.TrailingWelch"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.WindowRecord","page":"API reference","text":"WindowRecord\n\nOne scored window of a replay: window index, payload row_start and row_end, their mission times content_start and content_end, the arrival time complete_at of the completing_batch, the window's coverage, the classifier score, the decision, the inference wall time inference_wall_ms, and psd_row, the last delivered row behind the causal PSD estimate (TrailingWelch) the window was whitened with, 0 when the detector's static PSD was used, and release_at, the arrival time at which the window was scored: its complete_at for a Stateless scorer, and for a Stateful one the arrival that released it in content order (OrderedCommit). The twelve-argument constructor sets release_at = complete_at.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.WindowRecord"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#StreamingInference.WindowScheduler","page":"API reference","text":"WindowScheduler(window_size, step_size; min_coverage = 1.0, context_rows = 0, payload_rows = 0)\n\nBookkeeping of the sliding windows (window m covers rows [1 + (m − 1) S, (m − 1) S + W]) that have become evaluable: a window is evaluable once its own rows are all delivered and at least min_coverage of its conditioning stretch is, and each window is emitted once. A hole inside a window is never scored across; min_coverage below one only admits a window whose context is incomplete.\n\ncontext_rows is the conditioning stretch the detector needs on each side of a window: a window becomes evaluable only once that stretch, cut to the record by payload_rows (0 meaning unknown, so no cut at the end), is covered. The whitening is zero-phase and its kernel therefore two-sided, so a window scored before the data after it has arrived is not conditioned as the batch pipeline conditions it; matching that conditioning requires a lag of context_rows samples behind the delivery front.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.WindowScheduler"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.active_manifest_path-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"active_manifest_path() -> Union{Nothing, String}\n\nPath of the Manifest resolved for the active project, or nothing when the active project has none on disk. Candidates are searched in the directory of Base.active_project() in the order Julia itself applies: the version-specific Manifest-v<major>.<minor>.toml, JuliaManifest.toml, Manifest.toml.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.active_manifest_path"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.add!-Tuple{Coverage, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"add!(coverage, rows) -> Coverage\n\nMark rows as delivered, merging adjacent and overlapping intervals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.add!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.alarm_runs-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"alarm_runs(indices) -> Vector{UnitRange{Int}}\n\nMaximal runs of consecutive integers of the sorted vector indices, as ranges of positions into it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.alarm_runs"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.alert_latency_table-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, DataFrames.DataFrame, RunGeometry}","page":"API reference","text":"alert_latency_table(windows, events, geometry; processing_latency_hours = 1.0,\n                    persistence = 1, crediting = :signal) -> DataFrame\n\nPer event of events (columns merger_time_s [s after the mission epoch] and, when present, label_start_index/label_end_index payload rows; a label or event column names it): the earliest alert of windows (the table of replay_run) touching the event's credited span (rows, or the window containing the merger when no span is given).\n\ncrediting fixes where the credited span starts. With :signal it starts at the signal onset signal_start_index of the event table (the first window in which the source reaches the labelling SNR threshold) and ends with the label span: an alarm earlier in the label span cannot be caused by the source and counts as a false alarm. With :label the whole label span is credited, the convention of the training labels (96 h before to 27 min after the merger for the Isfan et al. (2025) spans), which credits noise alarms preceding the signal as early detections. A table with spans but without signal_start_index is refused under :signal.\n\nAn alert is a run of persistence consecutive alarmed windows — consecutive in window index, whatever order they reached the ground — at least one of which overlaps the span. It is raised by the arrival that completes the run: t_alarm is the latest time at which one of its windows was scored (scored_at: complete_at, or release_at for a stateful scorer) and alarm_window the window of that arrival. With persistence = 1 every alarmed window is an alert on its own. latency_data_h = t_alarm − t_merger (negative when the alert precedes the merger), latency_total_h = latency_data_h + processing_latency_hours, the inference wall time of the completing window, detected, and shared_alert, true when the same alert is also another event's (label spans that overlap). Runs of alarmed windows outside every label span that reach persistence are false-alarm episodes, reported as false_alarms_per_30d in every row; shorter runs raise no alert and are not counted. alert_persistence and alert_crediting record the criteria.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.alert_latency_table"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.analysis_band-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"analysis_band(section, key, default) -> Tuple{Float64,Float64}\n\nTwo-element ascending positive frequency band [Hz] from the configuration.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.analysis_band"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.ancestor_with_project-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"ancestor_with_project(dir; named = false) -> Union{Nothing,String}\n\nThe nearest of dir and its ancestors holding a Project.toml (with named = true, one that declares a package name), or nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.ancestor_with_project"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.animate_mission_replay","page":"API reference","text":"animate_mission_replay(windows, threshold, path; epoch, label_spans = nothing,\n                       span_label = \"Labelled span\", score_label = \"Score\",\n                       score_name = \"Window score\", score_range = nothing,\n                       n_frames = 200, framerate = 20, hold_frames = 20,\n                       max_points = 6000, size = figure_size(2, 2),\n                       px_per_unit = 2) -> String\n\nFour stacked panels of a telemetry replay, two main panels and two strips on a canvas of size [pt], on a shared mission-time axis [days since epoch, by default the content end of the first window]: window coverage, the window score (axis score_label, legend entry score_name, limits score_range or the range of the scores and the threshold widened by 5 %) with the decision threshold as a dashed rule, the alarmed windows marked, and the spans alerts are credited to (label_spans, pairs of DateTime, named span_label in the legend) shaded, the count of alarm episodes accumulated along mission time, and the availability latency of every window (complete_at − content_end [h]: the wait for its conditioning stretch and the downlink delay of the batch that completes it).\n\nThe windows are revealed in arrival order, sorted by complete_at, not in mission-time order: a pass delivers its backlog newest first and a window becomes evaluable only once the conditioning stretch around it has landed, so the trace fills in wherever windows have become evaluable rather than from left to right. A dotted rule marks the ground clock, whose distance to the data edge is the availability latency. The sweep takes about n_frames frames and the traces are decimated to about max_points windows, the alarmed ones always kept. windows is the table of replay_run, path must name a GIF, the only file written. Returns path. Requires CairoMakie to be loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.animate_mission_replay"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.animation_theme","page":"API reference","text":"animation_theme(; size = FIGURE_SIZE, fontsize = FIGURE_FONTSIZE)\n\nTheme of the animations: figure_theme unchanged, on a canvas snapped to an even whole number of typographic points so that every frame renders at exactly the size declared to the encoder. Requires CairoMakie to be loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.animation_theme"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.arrival_events","page":"API reference","text":"arrival_events(run) -> Vector{ArrivalEvent}\n\nThe arrival feed in mission-time order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.arrival_events"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.backup_existing!-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"backup_existing!(path) -> Union{Nothing, String}\n\nMove an existing file at path to <stem>_#k<ext> with the first free k ≥ 1 (the safesave convention of DrWatson), so that a new write at path never destroys a previous result. Returns the backup path, or nothing when there was nothing to move.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.backup_existing!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.batch_rows-Tuple{Integer, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"batch_rows(k, points_per_batch) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nPayload rows [(k − 1) P + 1, k P] of the global batch index k with P samples per batch (row-index exact in the producer's external mode).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.batch_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.cfgget-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"cfgget(section, key, default; type = Any, min = nothing, max = nothing, choices = nothing)\n\nRead key from a configuration section, falling back to default when the key is absent. Validates the value against an expected type, optional inclusive bounds, and an optional set of admissible choices, throwing an ArgumentError naming the offending key on any violation. Numeric values are converted to type when the conversion is exact.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.cfgget"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.channel_psds-Tuple{Any, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"channel_psds(psd, n_channels)\n\nThe whitening PSD of every channel of a multichannel stretch: psd is nothing (no whitening) or a collection of one PSD per channel. A single callable is refused, since the channels do not share a spectrum.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.channel_psds"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.check_band_edges-Tuple{Any}","page":"API reference","text":"check_band_edges(band_edges)\n\nValidates the edges of the :bands feature set: at least two strictly ascending positive frequencies [Hz]. Returns them as Vector{Float64}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.check_band_edges"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.check_frame_scale-Tuple{Real}","page":"API reference","text":"check_frame_scale(px_per_unit)\n\nThrow unless px_per_unit is a whole number at least one. A fractional raster scale renders frames that do not match the size declared to the video encoder, which appears as a band of noise along their top edge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.check_frame_scale"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.check_gif_path-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"check_gif_path(path)\n\nThrow unless path names a GIF; the animations of the project are written as GIF.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.check_gif_path"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.check_memory-Tuple{Real, NamedTuple}","page":"API reference","text":"check_memory(estimate_gib, resources; stage)\n\nEnforce the [resources] thresholds on a pre-flight estimate: throw an ArgumentError naming stage above max_memory_gib, warn above warn_memory_gib, otherwise log the estimate. Returns estimate_gib.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.check_memory"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.chronological_split-Tuple{Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"chronological_split(n; train_fraction = 0.7, validation_fraction = 0.15, buffer = 0)\n\nPartition n chronologically ordered windows into contiguous training, validation, and test blocks holding train_fraction, validation_fraction, and the remaining fraction of the windows, separated by buffer unused windows so that overlapping windows never straddle two blocks. Returns a named tuple of UnitRange{Int} (train, validation, test); every block must be non-empty.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.chronological_split"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.condition_window-Tuple{StreamingDetector, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"condition_window(detector, stretch, offset; psd = detector.psd) -> AbstractVecOrMat{Float64}\n\nThe window starting at offset (1-based) of the contiguous delivered stretch, conditioned as the batch pipeline conditions a record. A matrix stretch holds several synchronous channels, one per column; each is conditioned on its own with the PSD of its position in psd (channel_psds), and the window is returned as a matrix. For one channel: the stretch high-passed (highpass_record) and, unless psd is nothing, whitened by psd (whiten_record) as a whole, then the window cut from it. psd replaces the detector's whitening PSD for this window — in a replay under TrailingWelch, the causal PSD estimate, made only from data already delivered to the ground station.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.condition_window"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.conditioning_rows-Tuple{WindowScheduler, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"conditioning_rows(scheduler, m) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nPayload rows that must be delivered before window m can be scored: its own rows widened by context_rows on each side and cut to the record (payload_rows, when known). At the ends of a record the stretch cannot be centred on the window and the score is edge-affected, exactly as the first and last windows of a batch-processed record are.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.conditioning_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.config_root-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"config_root(path) -> String\n\nThe pipeline root of the configuration file at path: its [paths] root (relative to the file's directory) when given, otherwise the nearest directory above the file holding a Project.toml, otherwise project_root.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.config_root"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.content_digest-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"content_digest(path) -> String\n\nSHA-256 (hexadecimal) of the content of the file at path: the identity of an input product whatever its location or modification time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.content_digest"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.contiguous_runs-Tuple{AbstractVector{Bool}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"contiguous_runs(mask, windows) -> Vector{UnitRange{Int}}\n\nMaximal runs of true in mask over consecutive windows of a record: windows holds the record window index of every row, strictly increasing, and a run ends where the index jumps, at a gap of the record. nothing for windows is the case without gaps.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.contiguous_runs"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.contiguous_runs-Tuple{AbstractVector{Bool}}","page":"API reference","text":"contiguous_runs(mask) -> Vector{UnitRange{Int}}\n\nMaximal runs of true in mask, in order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.contiguous_runs"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.covered_fraction-Tuple{Coverage, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"covered_fraction(coverage, rows) -> Float64\n\nFraction of rows that are delivered.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.covered_fraction"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.covered_stretch-Tuple{Coverage, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"covered_stretch(coverage, rows) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nThe delivered interval containing every row of rows; empty when the rows are not fully delivered.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.covered_stretch"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.credited_span_label-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"credited_span_label(crediting) -> String\n\nLegend name of the spans alerts are credited to under crediting.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.credited_span_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.credited_span_starts-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"credited_span_starts(events, crediting) -> Union{Nothing,Vector{Int}}\n\nFirst payload rows of the credited spans of an event table: the column signal_start_index under crediting = :signal, label_start_index under :label; nothing when the table carries no label spans. Refuses a table with spans but without the signal onset under :signal, and onsets outside their label span.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.credited_span_starts"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.decade_label","page":"API reference","text":"decade_label(k, m = 1) -> String\n\nPlain-decimal tick label of m times 10^k for a single-digit mantissa m: 1, 10, 100, 0.1, 0.01; 20, 0.2, 0.05.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.decade_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.decimation-Tuple{Integer, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"decimation(n, max_points) -> StepRange\n\nIndex range keeping about max_points of n samples.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.decimation"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.declare_gap!-Tuple{ReplayState, GapEvent}","page":"API reference","text":"declare_gap!(state, gap::GapEvent)\n\nRecord gap, pass it to the stateful scorer (estimator_gap!), and move the release past it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.declare_gap!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.declare_gaps!-Tuple{ReplayState, Integer, Integer, Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"declare_gaps!(state, first_window, last_window, cause)\n\nDeclare the windows first_window:last_window as gaps: runs of windows that can never be scored (window_lost) with cause :lost, the others with cause.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.declare_gaps!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.delivered_rows-Tuple{ReplayState, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"API reference","text":"delivered_rows(state, rows) -> Vector{Float32} or Matrix{Float32}\n\nThe payload of the delivered rows rows, assembled from the batches on the ground by the rows they hold (ArgumentError when a row is not covered); a matrix with one column per channel when the run delivers several.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.delivered_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.delivered_stretch-Tuple{ReplayState, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"API reference","text":"delivered_stretch(state, window) -> (samples, offset)\n\nThe delivered samples around window — the covered interval containing it, cut to context_windows window lengths on each side — and the 1-based offset of the window inside them; (nothing, 0) when the window is not fully delivered.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.delivered_stretch"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.dense_log_ticks-Tuple{Real, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"dense_log_ticks(lo, hi) -> (values, labels)\n\nTicks of a logarithmic axis spanning [lo, hi] at the 1×, 2× and 5× multiples of every decade, for axes that span two or three decades; above nine such ticks it falls back to log_ticks.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.dense_log_ticks"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.detector_step-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API reference","text":"detector_step(windows) -> Int\n\nWindow step [samples] implied by a replay table: the smallest positive difference between distinct row_start values (windows complete out of order, so the table is not sorted by window), or the window length when a single window was scored.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.detector_step"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.edge_margin_windows-Tuple{NamedTuple}","page":"API reference","text":"edge_margin_windows(settings) -> Int\n\nNumber of windows dropped at each end of a record for the edge_margin of the [preprocessing] settings, given in window lengths: round(edge_margin * window_size / step_size).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.edge_margin_windows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.estimator_gap!-Tuple{AbstractWindowEstimator, GapEvent}","page":"API reference","text":"estimator_gap!(estimator, gap::GapEvent)\n\nInform a Stateful estimator that the windows of gap will not be seen, before the first window after it; the estimator decides whether to reset, bridge, or record the hole. A no-op unless an estimator implements it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.estimator_gap!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.estimator_memory-Tuple{AbstractWindowEstimator}","page":"API reference","text":"estimator_memory(estimator) -> EstimatorMemory\n\nStateless unless an estimator declares otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.estimator_memory"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.event_merger_times-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API reference","text":"event_merger_times(events) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nMerger times [s after the mission epoch] of an event table: the column merger_time_s (LDC event tables) or t_c_sec (the simulator catalogue).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.event_merger_times"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.event_metrics-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"event_metrics(decisions, labels; step_size, sample_rate, windows = nothing) -> NamedTuple\n\nWindow-level and event-level detection statistics of binary decisions against binary labels over chronologically ordered windows advanced by step_size samples at sample_rate [Hz]:\n\nprecision, recall, fpr (the false-positive rate, i.e. the alarm duty cycle on unlabelled windows), f1, balanced_accuracy at window level (NaN where undefined);\nn_events: contiguous runs of positive labels; n_detected: events with at least one alarm inside their run; event_recall;\nn_false_alarm_episodes: contiguous runs of alarmed windows outside the labelled spans (an alarm that covers an event and extends beyond it contributes its unlabelled excess, so a permanently raised alarm is not free of false alarms); observation_days; false_alarms_per_30d, the operational false-alarm rate.\n\nFor a table of a record with gaps, windows gives the record window index of every row (window_indices): events and false-alarm episodes then end at a gap instead of running across it (contiguous_runs). The observation time is that of the rows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.event_metrics"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.event_symbol-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"event_symbol(value) -> Symbol\n\n:ingested, :retry, :lost, or :pruned for the producer's event values, :other for anything else (tolerated, ignored).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.event_symbol"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.extract_features","page":"API reference","text":"extract_features(x, sample_rate = 0.2; low_band = (1e-3, 5e-3),\n                 high_band = (5e-3, 1e-1), band_edges = nothing, taper = :hann,\n                 feature_set = :whitened, combination = :mean)\n\nFeature vector of a window x sampled at sample_rate [Hz], computed from its tapered periodogram P_k (tapered_periodogram). Returns a tuple of Float32 whose entries are named by feature_names.\n\nA matrix x holds a window of several synchronous channels, one per column, and combination says how they enter; either way the number of features does not depend on the number of channels.\n\n:mean (default): the features of the channel-averaged periodogram (network_periodogram), the excess power of the network. It is the best incoherent statistic for a signal split equally between the channels, and dilutes one that a single channel sees: its excess power is divided by the number of channels while the noise spread falls only as the root of it.\n:max: the features of every channel, combined by the value that lies farthest towards a signal — the largest band power and power spread (and, for :paper, mean and maximum), the smallest entropy. A signal seen by one channel keeps its features; the noise level of a maximum over C channels is higher than that of one, a trials factor.\n\nfeature_set = :whitened (the default) expects a window of the whitened record (whiten_record), whose periodogram has unit mean for noise and is therefore independent of window length and noise amplitude:\n\nmean whitened power in low_band [Hz];\nmean whitened power in high_band [Hz];\nspectral entropy of the normalised whitened power, divided by ln N_mathrmbins so that it lies in 0 1;\nlog_10 of the standard deviation of the whitened power (0 for white noise, whose periodogram is exponentially distributed).\n\nfeature_set = :bands generalises the whitened set to the bands between consecutive band_edges [Hz] (the first band closed on both sides, the others open at their lower edge): the mean whitened power of every band, then the entropy and the log power spread as above — `length(band_edges)\n\n1features. With the edges[1e-3, 5e-3, 1e-1]` it reproduces the\n\nwhitened set exactly.\n\nfeature_set = :paper is the set of Isfan et al. (2025) on the raw window: the normalised spectral entropy and log_10 of the mean, standard deviation, and maximum of the periodogram (the paper uses the raw moments; the logarithm is a monotone transform that keeps their min–max scaling well conditioned over the many decades a noise spectrum can span).\n\nThrows an ArgumentError when an analysis band holds no frequency bin.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.extract_features"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.extract_features-Tuple{FeatureMap, AbstractVecOrMat{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"extract_features(map::FeatureMap, window, sample_rate) -> Tuple\n\nFeatures of window under the set and bands of map.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.extract_features"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.feature_geometry-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"feature_geometry(features_path, config) -> NamedTuple\n\nWindow geometry (window_size, step_size, sample_rate, and first_window, the record window index of the table's first row, above 1 when an edge margin was dropped) of a feature table, read from the sidecar <stem>.toml written beside it by the pre-processor; falls back to the [preprocessing] section with a warning when the sidecar is absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.feature_geometry"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.feature_names-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"feature_names(feature_set; n_bands = 2) -> Vector{Symbol}\n\nColumn names of the feature table produced by extract_features for feature_set; n_bands is the number of bands of the :bands set (one less than the number of edges) and is ignored otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.feature_names"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_roc","page":"API reference","text":"figure_roc(fpr, tpr, auc; label = nothing) -> Figure\n\nReceiver operating characteristic with the chance diagonal and the area under the curve stated in the legend, after the scorer's name label when given. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_roc"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_score_distribution","page":"API reference","text":"figure_score_distribution(probabilities, threshold; labels = nothing, n_bins = 50,\n                          score_label = \"Score\", score_range = nothing) -> Figure\n\nHistogram of the window scores, split into noise and labelled windows when labels is given, with the decision threshold. The bins span score_range, by default the range of the scores and the threshold widened by 5 %; the axis is labelled score_label. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_score_distribution"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_sensitivity","page":"API reference","text":"figure_sensitivity(snrs, labels, decisions; n_bins = 8) -> Figure\n\nFraction of positive windows detected per matched-filter SNR bin, with the number of windows per bin annotated. Returns nothing when no positive window exists. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_sensitivity"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_size","page":"API reference","text":"figure_size(main_panels = 1, strips = 0) -> Tuple{Int,Int}\n\nCanvas [pt] of a figure with main_panels stacked main panels and strips auxiliary strips: FIGURE_SIZE heightened by PANEL_HEIGHT per panel beyond the first and STRIP_HEIGHT per strip.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_size"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_telemetry_alerts","page":"API reference","text":"figure_telemetry_alerts(windows, threshold; epoch, label_spans = nothing,\n                        latencies = nothing, span_label = \"Labelled span\",\n                        score_label = \"Score\", score_name = \"Window score\",\n                        event_label = \"Event time\", score_range = nothing) -> Figure\n\nTwo stacked panels on a shared mission-time axis [days since epoch] for the windows table of a replay: the score of every window at its content end (axis score_label, legend entry score_name, limits score_range or the range of the scores and the threshold widened by 5 %) with the decision threshold, alarmed windows marked, and the spans alerts are credited to (label_spans, pairs of DateTime, named span_label in the legend) shaded; below, the ground-availability latency of every window (complete_at − content_end [h]) with the alert latencies of the detected events (latencies, the table of alert_latency_table, their event times named event_label) annotated. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_telemetry_alerts"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_theme","page":"API reference","text":"figure_theme(; size = FIGURE_SIZE, fontsize = FIGURE_FONTSIZE)\n\nMakie theme of the base layout: Computer Modern fonts, boxed axes with inward ticks, dashed low-opacity grid, no minor ticks, 3 pt data lines, 14 pt markers with a 1.5 pt stroke, and the canvas size in typographic points, so that a PDF export enters a document at native size. Taller canvases come from figure_size. Requires CairoMakie to be loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_theme"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.figure_threshold_sweep","page":"API reference","text":"figure_threshold_sweep(sweep, threshold; target_far_per_30d = nothing,\n                       operating_point = nothing) -> Figure\n\nEvent-level operating characteristic of a scored block: two stacked panels over the decision threshold, the event recall (solid) with the window recall (dashed), and the false-alarm episodes per 30 days on a logarithmic axis (thresholds without a false alarm are left blank). The operating point threshold is marked and the target_far_per_30d of the far criterion drawn when given. operating_point, anything carrying n_detected, n_events, and false_alarms_per_30d, puts the metrics of the applied threshold in the legend; they cannot be read off sweep, whose candidates are score quantiles and are sparse in the far tail. Without it the legend states the threshold alone. sweep is the table of threshold_sweep. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.figure_threshold_sweep"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.finalize_replay!-Tuple{ReplayState}","page":"API reference","text":"finalize_replay!(state; on_window = nothing)\n\nClose a replay at the end of its arrival feed: for a Stateful scorer, release every held window in content order and declare the windows still missing, up to the last window of the record when its length is known, as :undelivered gaps. A no-op for a Stateless scorer. Returns the windows released.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.finalize_replay!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.finite_stretches-Tuple{Vararg{AbstractVector{<:Real}}}","page":"API reference","text":"finite_stretches(columns...; shortest = 1) -> Vector{UnitRange{Int}}\n\nMaximal runs of rows at which every one of the columns (vectors of one length) is finite, in order: the stretches of a record between its gaps, whose samples are marked by NaN. Runs of fewer than shortest rows are dropped.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.finite_stretches"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.fixed_spans-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, Real, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"fixed_spans(event_indices, fs, n; before, after) -> Vector{UnitRange{Int}}\n\nSample ranges [i - before·fs, i + after·fs] around the event sample indices, clipped to 1:n (before, after in seconds); the label window of Isfan et al. (2025, doi:10.1088/1361-6382/ae1787) around a binary merger, for example, is before = 4 d, after = 27 min.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.fixed_spans"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.follow_run-Tuple{AbstractTelemetryRun, StreamingDetector}","page":"API reference","text":"follow_run(run, detector; poll_interval_sec = 1.0, min_coverage = 1.0,\n           tdi_gap_dilation_sec = 0.0, trailing_psd = nothing,\n           order_horizon = nothing, late_policy = :skip,\n           on_window = nothing, max_wall_sec = Inf) -> DataFrame\n\nLive mode: poll the arrival feed of run every poll_interval_sec, consuming events beyond those already processed, until the run reaches a terminal state (run_state ≠ :active) and the feed is drained, or max_wall_sec of wall time elapse. The consumer never writes into the run. A stateful scorer is served in content order as in replay_run; the replay is finalised (finalize_replay!) when the loop ends. Returns the windows_table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.follow_run"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.frame_schedule-Tuple{Integer, Integer, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"frame_schedule(n, n_frames, hold_frames) -> Vector{Int}\n\nSweep of about n_frames states out of n, always ending on n, followed by hold_frames repetitions of the last state. The sweep starts at two states, since a single one draws no line segment.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.frame_schedule"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.gaps_table-Tuple{ReplayState}","page":"API reference","text":"gaps_table(state) -> DataFrame\n\nThe GapEvents of a stateful replay, one row each: first_window, last_window, cause, declared_at; empty for a Stateless scorer.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.gaps_table"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.git_provenance-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"git_provenance() -> Dict{String, Any}\n\nGit description of the pipeline root (project_root, DrWatson.gitdescribe), whether the tree is dirty, the version of the package at the root (package_version, from its Project.toml), and the version of this package (streaminference_version); \"unknown\" for the commit and true for the dirty flag when the tree's state cannot be established (outside a git repository, or without git).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.git_provenance"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.git_state-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"git_state(dir) -> (commit, dirty)\n\nDrWatson.gitdescribe of the repository holding dir and whether its tree is dirty; \"unknown\" and true when the state cannot be established (outside a git repository, or without git).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.git_state"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.hardware_fingerprint-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"hardware_fingerprint() -> Dict{String, Any}\n\nPlatform fingerprint recorded in run provenance snapshots: an anonymous machine identifier (machine_id), OS kernel, CPU model and logical core count, total memory, Julia version with the sanitised versioninfo() output (sanitized_versioninfo), and thread/worker counts (Julia threads, BLAS threads, Distributed workers). Together with the configuration snapshot and the git description this makes every result attributable to configuration, code version, and hardware. The host's name never enters a snapshot. GPU fields are to be appended once a functional GPU backend is part of the pipeline.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.hardware_fingerprint"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.highpass_record-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"highpass_record(x, fs; cutoff, order = 8) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nZero-phase high-pass filtering of the whole record x sampled at fs [Hz] in the frequency domain, with the Butterworth magnitude response H(f) = 1 + (f_c  f)^2p^-12 of cutoff cutoff = f_c [Hz] and order order = p (H(0) = 0). cutoff = 0 returns a copy of x. Where the noise rises steeply towards low frequencies (red noise, such as the acceleration noise propto f^-6 of a space-borne interferometer below 0.4 mHz), a record must be high-passed below the analysis bands before it is cut into windows; otherwise the sub-window drift leaks into every band through any taper.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.highpass_record"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.hold_window!-Tuple{ReplayState, Integer, UnitRange{Int64}, AbstractVecOrMat{<:Real}, Integer, Any, Integer, ArrivalEvent, BatchRecord}","page":"API reference","text":"hold_window!(state, m, window, stretch, offset, psd, psd_row, event, batch)\n\nCondition the evaluable window m of a replay with a Stateful scorer and hold it for its ordered release; a window whose gap was already declared is late (OrderedCommit).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.hold_window!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.holes-Tuple{Coverage, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"holes(coverage, rows) -> Vector{UnitRange{Int}}\n\nSub-intervals of rows that are not delivered, in order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.holes"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.inference_settings-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"inference_settings(config) -> NamedTuple\n\nValidated [inference] parameters: feature and label tables, block selection, and the window geometry used when a feature table has no sidecar.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.inference_settings"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.interpolated_psd-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"interpolated_psd(freqs, psd) -> Function\n\nCallable f mapsto S(f) interpolating the tabulated one-sided PSD psd at the strictly increasing positive frequencies freqs linearly in log f–log S, constant outside the tabulated range, and Inf for f le 0 (so whitening sets the DC bin to zero).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.interpolated_psd"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.label_bands!","page":"API reference","text":"label_bands!(axis, x, labels)\n\nShaded band over every contiguous run of positive labels along x; the first band carries the legend entry. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.label_bands!"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.layer_provenance","page":"API reference","text":"layer_provenance(manifest = active_manifest_path()) -> Vector{Dict{String, Any}}\n\nThe packages of the resolved environment that make up the pipeline: this package and every package whose dependencies reach it, as the Manifest at manifest records them. Each entry holds the name and version and, according to how the package is tracked, its tree_hash (registered or tracked by URL), url and revision (tracked by URL), or its path with the git_commit and git_dirty state of that directory (tracked by path). This package comes first, the others follow by name. Empty without a Manifest on disk.\n\nThe git description of the pipeline root (git_provenance) covers one repository; a pipeline assembled from several packages is attributed to code only by the revision of each.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.layer_provenance"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.linear_interpolation-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"linear_interpolation(x, y, xq) -> Float64\n\nValue at xq of the piecewise-linear interpolant of y over the strictly increasing abscissae x, constant beyond the ends.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.linear_interpolation"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.list_batches","page":"API reference","text":"list_batches(run) -> Vector{BatchRecord}\n\nEvery batch known to the run (delivered, lost, or pruned), sorted by index.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.list_batches"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.load_config-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"load_config(path) -> Dict{String, Any}\n\nParse the TOML configuration at path, failing fast when the file is absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.load_config"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.load_data-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"load_data(feature_path, label_path) -> (X, y, df_labels)\n\nRaw feature matrix, integer label vector, and the full label table (which retains auxiliary columns such as SNR) from the CSVs written by scripts/preprocess_ldc.jl.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.load_data"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.load_features-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"load_features(feature_path) -> Matrix{Float32}\n\nRaw feature matrix (samples × features) from a feature CSV written by a pre-processing stage. Any encoding for an estimator is a separate step, so that a scaler fitted on the training partition is applied identically at inference.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.load_features"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.log_ticks-Tuple{Real, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"log_ticks(lo, hi) -> (values, labels)\n\nTick values of a logarithmic axis spanning [lo, hi]: the decades inside the range, with the 2× and 5× intermediates added when fewer than two decades fall inside, labelled as plain decimals.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.log_ticks"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.machine_id-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"machine_id() -> String\n\nStable anonymous identifier of the host: the first twelve hexadecimal characters of the SHA-256 digest of its name. Two runs on the same machine share it and runs on different machines do not, which is what provenance needs, while the machine's name — which is personal data in a published artifact — is not recoverable from it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.machine_id"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.manifest_sha256-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"manifest_sha256() -> String\n\nSHA-256 digest (hexadecimal) of the active Manifest (active_manifest_path), or \"unknown\" when there is none. The digest identifies the resolved dependency state of a run without carrying the file into every record.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.manifest_sha256"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.matched_filter_snr-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"matched_filter_snr(h, fs; psd)\n\nOptimal matched-filter signal-to-noise ratio of the series h sampled at fs [Hz] against the one-sided noise PSD psd(f):\n\nrho^2 = 4 int_0^infty fractilde h(f)^2S_n(f)  mathrmdf\n       approx 4 Delta f sum_k ge 1 fractilde h(f_k)^2S_n(f_k)\n\nwith tilde h(f_k) = Delta t sum_j h_j e^-2pi i f_k t_j and Delta f = f_s  n. The DC bin is excluded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.matched_filter_snr"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.network_periodogram-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"network_periodogram(x; taper = :hann) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nTapered periodogram of a window (tapered_periodogram); for a matrix x of C synchronous channels, one per column, the average over the channels, bar P_k = frac1C sum_c P_k^(c). On channels whitened one by one, with independent noise, every P_k^(c) has unit mean under noise and bar P_k keeps it while its variance falls as 1C; the power of a signal adds over the channels, as the squared signal-to-noise ratios of a network do.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.network_periodogram"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.new_run_id-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"new_run_id() -> String\n\nEight-character run identifier drawn from a UUID.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.new_run_id"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.newly_evaluable!-Tuple{WindowScheduler, Coverage, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"newly_evaluable!(scheduler, coverage, rows) -> Vector{Int}\n\nWindows whose conditioning stretch (conditioning_rows) intersects rows and is now covered under coverage, and that have not been emitted before; they are recorded as emitted. An arriving batch can therefore make a window evaluable that lies up to context_rows earlier in the record, which is why the search range is widened.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.newly_evaluable!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.override-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"override(cli_value, cfg_value)\n\nPrecedence of an explicit command-line value over the configuration: cli_value unless it is nothing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.override"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.parameter_digest-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"parameter_digest(parameters) -> String\n\nSHA-256 (hexadecimal) of the key-sorted TOML rendering of a parameter dictionary: the identity of the parameters of a product, the same in every process and on every machine (unlike Base.hash, which also differs between Julia versions). It is as stable as the TOML rendering: a change of the TOML printer would change it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.parameter_digest"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.parse_batch_name-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"parse_batch_name(name) -> (index, live)\n\nGlobal batch index and live flag of a batch directory name LIVE_batch_<k> or ARCH_batch_<k>; ArgumentError for any other form.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.parse_batch_name"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.pipeline_paths-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"pipeline_paths(config) -> NamedTuple\n\nOutput roots of the pipeline from the [paths] section — inputs, models, plots, results — resolved against the package root. Absent keys fall back to the standard tree (data/inputs, models, data/outputs/plots, data/outputs/results).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.pipeline_paths"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.place_signal!-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Integer, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"place_signal!(record, signal, anchor_index, signal_anchor) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nAdd signal into record so that signal[signal_anchor] lands on record[anchor_index], dropping the parts of signal that fall outside the record. Returns the range of record indices that received the signal (empty when nothing overlaps).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.place_signal!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.process_event!-Tuple{ReplayState, AbstractTelemetryRun, ArrivalEvent}","page":"API reference","text":"process_event!(state, run, event; on_window = nothing) -> Vector{WindowRecord}\n\nConsume one arrival event: an ingested batch is read, added to the coverage, and every window that thereby becomes evaluable is conditioned; a lost or pruned batch is removed from the coverage with the configured erosion on each side. Other events are ignored. A Stateless scorer scores the evaluable windows at the event's mission time; for a Stateful one they are held and the event releases, in content order, every held window that no earlier window still waits for (OrderedCommit), which may include windows completed by earlier events. Returns the windows scored by this event; on_window(record) is called for each.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.process_event!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.product_table-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"product_table(kind; channels, parents = Dict{String,Any}(), schema = 1) -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nThe [product] table of a sidecar: the kind of product (\"features\", \"labels\", …), the channels it was made from (a channel-set token such as \"A\"), the schema version of its tables, and the content digests (content_digest) of its parents, so that a product can be traced to its inputs and refused when they do not match.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.product_table"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.project_root-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"project_root() -> String\n\nThe pipeline root: the directory every relative path of a configuration resolves against and whose repository the provenance records. In order: the root set by with_pipeline_root; the environment variable STREAMINGINFERENCE_ROOT; the nearest directory above the active environment whose Project.toml declares a package (the scripts/, test/, docs/ and bench/ environments of a pipeline resolve to its repository). Throws an ArgumentError when none applies, rather than resolving against the directory of an installed package.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.project_root"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.provenance-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"provenance() -> Dict{String, Any}\n\nhardware, git, layers, and environment sections of a provenance snapshot, plus the wall-clock time of writing. layers lists the packages of the pipeline with their revisions (layer_provenance); environment names the active project and the digest of its Manifest (manifest_sha256).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.provenance"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.provenance_path-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"provenance_path(p) -> String\n\np as recorded in a provenance snapshot: relative to project_root when it lies inside it, and otherwise its file name alone. A path outside the package root belongs to the machine that ran the stage, not to the run, and carries the account name and the directory layout of that machine into artifacts that are meant to be published; the file name is what identifies the input. Use rootrelative instead wherever the recorded path is read back and resolved rather than only reported.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.provenance_path"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.read_batch","page":"API reference","text":"read_batch(run, name) -> Vector{Float32}\n\nPayload samples of the delivered batch name, its segments concatenated in ascending segment id: a vector, or for a run of several synchronous channels a matrix with one column per channel (the delivery of a batch is common to its channels).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.read_batch"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.record_memory_estimate_gib-Tuple{Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"record_memory_estimate_gib(n_samples; copies = 6) -> Float64\n\nPre-flight estimate of the memory of processing a record of n_samples double-precision samples through the high-pass, whitening, and windowing chain, which holds about copies record-length arrays (time series, its transform, and intermediates).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.record_memory_estimate_gib"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.recorded_channels-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"recorded_channels(table_path; default) -> String\n\nThe channel set a product was made from, as the sidecar of the table at table_path records it (<stem>.toml beside <stem>.csv): channels of its [product] table (product_table), else of [features]. default is returned for a table without a sidecar or whose sidecar names no channel set, as the products made before the channel sets were recorded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.recorded_channels"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.release_windows!-Tuple{ReplayState, Dates.DateTime, Any, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"release_windows!(state, t, scored, on_window)\n\nRelease the held windows of a stateful replay in content order at mission time t: score every window from the next index on that is held, declare a GapEvent over every run of windows that can never be scored or has outlived the order horizon, and stop at the first window that may still arrive (OrderedCommit).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.release_windows!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.remove!-Tuple{Coverage, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"remove!(coverage, rows) -> Coverage\n\nMark rows as no longer available (a pruned payload).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.remove!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.replay_run-Tuple{AbstractTelemetryRun, StreamingDetector}","page":"API reference","text":"replay_run(run, detector; min_coverage = 1.0, tdi_gap_dilation_sec = 0.0,\n           trailing_psd = nothing, order_horizon = nothing, late_policy = :skip,\n           on_window = nothing) -> DataFrame\n\nReplay the arrival feed of run in mission-time order through process_event! and return the windows_table: one row per scored window with window, row_start, row_end, content_start, content_end, complete_at, completing_batch, coverage, score, decision, inference_wall_ms, psd_row (and release_at for a Stateful scorer, whose windows are released in content order under order_horizon and late_policy; OrderedCommit). trailing_psd, a TrailingWelch, whitens every window by a causal PSD estimate instead of the detector's static PSD. The gaps of a stateful replay are read from replay_state.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.replay_run"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.replay_state-Tuple{AbstractTelemetryRun, StreamingDetector}","page":"API reference","text":"replay_state(run, detector; min_coverage = 1.0, tdi_gap_dilation_sec = 0.0,\n             trailing_psd = nothing, order_horizon = nothing, late_policy = :skip,\n             on_window = nothing) -> ReplayState\n\nThe ReplayState after the whole arrival feed of run, finalised (finalize_replay!): windows_table and gaps_table read from it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.replay_state"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.report_timing","page":"API reference","text":"report_timing(io = stdout)\n\nPrint the stage-timing table of TIMER.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.report_timing"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.reset_estimator!-Tuple{AbstractWindowEstimator}","page":"API reference","text":"reset_estimator!(estimator)\n\nReturn a Stateful estimator to its initial state; a replay calls it once before its first window. A no-op unless an estimator implements it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.reset_estimator!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.resolvepath-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"resolvepath(p) -> String\n\np resolved against project_root unless it is already absolute.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.resolvepath"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.resource_settings-Tuple{AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"resource_settings(config) -> NamedTuple\n\nMemory-safety thresholds of the [resources] section in GiB: max_memory_gib (a stage whose estimate exceeds it refuses to start; default half of the machine's memory) and warn_memory_gib (a warning; default a quarter).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.resource_settings"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.roc_auc-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"roc_auc(fpr, tpr)\n\nArea under the ROC curve by the trapezoidal rule; NaN when a rate is undefined.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.roc_auc"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.roc_curve-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"roc_curve(y, scores) -> (fpr, tpr, thresholds)\n\nReceiver operating characteristic of binary labels y (0/1) under the decision score >= threshold, evaluated at every distinct score in descending order and at +Inf (no alarms). fpr and tpr are non-decreasing; a class without members yields NaN rates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.roc_curve"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.root_package_version-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"root_package_version(root) -> String\n\nVersion declared in the Project.toml of the pipeline root root, or \"unknown\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.root_package_version"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.rootrelative-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"rootrelative(p) -> String\n\np expressed relative to project_root when it lies inside it, otherwise the absolute path unchanged; used when persisting paths in provenance snapshots so that run artifacts stay portable across machines.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.rootrelative"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.row_time-Tuple{RunGeometry, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"row_time(geometry, row) -> DateTime\n\nMission time of payload row row: start_sim_time + (row − 1) / sample_rate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.row_time"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.run_geometry","page":"API reference","text":"run_geometry(run) -> RunGeometry\n\nSampling and batching geometry of run.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.run_geometry"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.run_state","page":"API reference","text":"run_state(run) -> Symbol\n\n:active, :complete, or :aborted from the run's lifecycle sentinels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.run_state"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.sanitized_versioninfo-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"sanitized_versioninfo() -> String\n\nInteractiveUtils.versioninfo() output with the user's home directory replaced by ~. The Environment: block echoes every JULIA_* variable, several of which customarily hold paths under the home directory and with it the account name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.sanitized_versioninfo"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.save_animation","page":"API reference","text":"save_animation(render, stem; run_id = \"\") -> String\n\nWrite the animation <stem>.gif by calling render(path) with that path and write the provenance sidecar <stem>.toml (run identifier, frame_px, the pixel size of the written GIF, px_per_unit, file size, git description, hardware fingerprint, time), as save_figure does for a static figure. An existing GIF is backed up first. Returns the written path. Requires CairoMakie to be loaded.\n\nExample\n\nsave_animation(joinpath(plot_dir, \"training_history\"); run_id = run_id) do path\n    animate_training_history(history, path)\nend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.save_animation"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.save_figure","page":"API reference","text":"save_figure(figure, stem; run_id = \"\", formats = (\"pdf\", \"png\"), px_per_unit = 4)\n\nExport figure as <stem>.pdf (vector) and <stem>.png (raster at px_per_unit times the design size) and write the provenance sidecar <stem>.toml (run identifier, the canvas actually exported size_pt [pt], px_per_unit, git description, hardware fingerprint, time). Existing files are backed up first. Returns the vector of written paths. Requires CairoMakie to be loaded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.save_figure"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.scale_to_snr-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"scale_to_snr(h, fs, ρ_target; psd)\n\nh rescaled so that its matched_filter_snr equals ρ_target.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.scale_to_snr"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.score_bounds-Tuple{AbstractWindowScorer}","page":"API reference","text":"score_bounds(scorer) -> Tuple{Float64,Float64}\n\nRange of the score; (0.0, 1.0) unless a scorer declares otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.score_bounds"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.score_label-Tuple{AbstractWindowScorer}","page":"API reference","text":"score_label(scorer) -> String\n\nAxis label of the score in figures; \"Score\" unless a scorer declares otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.score_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.score_limits-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"score_limits(scores, threshold, score_range) -> (lo, hi)\n\nLimits of a score axis: score_range when given, otherwise the range of the finite scores and the threshold widened by 5 % on each side (by 0.05 when the range is a single value).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.score_limits"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.score_window-Tuple{StreamingDetector, AbstractVecOrMat{<:Real}, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"score_window(detector, stretch, offset; psd = detector.psd) -> Float32\n\nScore of the window starting at offset of the contiguous delivered stretch: the window conditioned (condition_window) and scored by the detector's scorer (window_score).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.score_window"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.scored_at-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API reference","text":"scored_at(windows) -> Vector{DateTime}\n\nThe arrival time at which every window of a replay table was scored: its release_at when the table has one (a Stateful scorer, whose windows wait for their predecessors), its complete_at otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.scored_at"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.section-Tuple{AbstractDict, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"section(config, name) -> Dict{String, Any}\n\nThe table name of config, or an empty table when absent.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.section"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.select_threshold-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"select_threshold(y, scores; criterion = \"far\", target_far_per_30d = 3.0,\n                 target_fpr = 0.05, step_size, sample_rate, n_candidates = 400)\n    -> (threshold, info)\n\nDecision threshold fitted on a calibration block of labels y and scores from the event-level operating characteristic threshold_sweep; threshold_rows selects the rows of that block:\n\n\"far\": the operating point of an alert trigger. A candidate is admissible when its false-alarm episode rate does not exceed target_far_per_30d and its window false-positive rate (the alarm duty cycle on unlabelled windows) does not exceed target_fpr. The candidates are scanned from the highest downwards and the threshold is the lowest candidate of the admissible range that starts at the top — the highest recall reachable while alarms remain short and isolated. The scan direction matters because the episode count is not monotone in the threshold: as the threshold falls, spurious episodes first multiply and then merge into a permanently raised alarm counted as a few long episodes, which an ascending scan would accept.\n\"fpr\": the lowest threshold whose window false-positive rate does not exceed target_fpr (monotone, so the scan direction is immaterial).\n\"youden\": the maximiser of tpr - fpr (requires both classes).\n\nWhen the block holds no positive window, \"youden\" falls back to \"fpr\" with a warning; the other criteria depend on negatives only. A block without negatives makes every candidate admissible for \"far\" and \"fpr\". info records the criterion applied, the targets, the rates on the fitting block at the threshold (fit_*), and the block size. Among them fit_false_alarm_episodes is the count the fitted rate rests on: its inverse square root is the relative error of that rate, and an operating point placed on a handful of episodes does not transfer to another record.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.select_threshold"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.smooth_psd-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"smooth_psd(freqs, psd, sigma_dex) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nThe one-sided PSD psd tabulated at the strictly increasing positive frequencies freqs, smoothed in log-frequency: log_10 S is averaged with Gaussian weights of standard deviation sigma_dex in log_10 f, each bin weighted by the log-frequency interval it spans (propto 1f on a uniform frequency grid), evaluated on a uniform log-frequency grid of step sigma_dex / 5 with the kernel truncated at four standard deviations, and read back at freqs by linear interpolation. Where the table is coarser than the kernel — its lowest bins — the grid interpolates the table instead. sigma_dex = 0 returns the table unchanged.\n\nA Welch estimate carries line-to-line scatter and resolves sharp spectral features, such as the notches of an instrument transfer function; the inverse square root of such a spectrum has a long, ringing impulse response, so whitening by it spreads every sample over many window lengths. Smoothing on scales narrower than any analysis band removes that fine structure and shortens the kernel accordingly.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.smooth_psd"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.snapshot_manifest-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"snapshot_manifest(dir) -> Union{Nothing, String}\n\nCopy the active Manifest (active_manifest_path) to <dir>/manifest_snapshot.toml, backing up an existing snapshot first (backup_existing!), and return the path written; nothing, with a warning, when the active project has no Manifest. Manifests are not tracked in the repository, so this copy is what pins the resolved environment of a run.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.snapshot_manifest"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.span_labels-Tuple{Integer, AbstractVector{<:AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}}","page":"API reference","text":"span_labels(n, spans) -> Vector{Int}\n\nPoint-wise labels of length n: 1 inside any of the sample ranges spans, 0 elsewhere.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.span_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.synthesize_noise-Tuple{Random.AbstractRNG, Integer, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"synthesize_noise(rng, n, fs; psd, f_min = 0.0) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nn samples of zero-mean stationary Gaussian noise at sampling frequency fs [Hz] whose one-sided power spectral density is psd(f) [Hz⁻¹]. The spectral coefficients are drawn as complex normals scaled to EX_k^2 = S(f_k) f_s n  2 (the unnormalised rfft convention), the DC bin is zeroed, and the Nyquist bin of an even n is forced real, so the inverse transform is a real series with the correct absolute amplitude. Bins below f_min [Hz] are left empty: a sensitivity model fitted over a band would, extrapolated towards zero frequency, put a drift many orders of magnitude above the in-band level into the record.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.synthesize_noise"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.tapered_periodogram-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"tapered_periodogram(x; taper = :hann) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nOne-sided periodogram of the window x after multiplication by the taper v: P_k = mathrmFFT(x v)_k^2  (n overlinev^2) with overlinev^2 the mean square of the taper, so that E P_k = sigma^2 for white noise of variance sigma^2 (unit mean on the output of whiten_record). The DC bin is set to zero. taper is :hann (default) or :none.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.tapered_periodogram"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.threshold_rows-Tuple{NamedTuple, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"threshold_rows(blocks, threshold_block) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nRows of the training table on which the decision threshold is fitted, given the blocks of chronological_split:\n\n\"validation\": the validation block alone, the classical split.\n\"held_out\": validation and test together, including the buffer windows between them so that the range stays contiguous in mission time and an alarm episode spanning the join is counted once.\n\nThe pooled block doubles the mission time behind the fitted false-alarm rate, whose relative error scales as the inverse square root of the episodes it counts; a 55-day block routinely counts fewer than five. The test block carries no information the fit could leak, being scored once after training and entering neither model selection nor early stopping, but it ceases to be an independent check of the operating point — that role belongs to a separate observation record.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.threshold_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.threshold_sweep-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"threshold_sweep(y, scores; step_size, sample_rate, n_candidates = 400) -> DataFrame\n\nWindow- and event-level detection statistics (event_metrics) of the decision score >= threshold at every candidate threshold, the n_candidates quantiles of scores in ascending order: one row per candidate with threshold, precision, recall, fpr, n_events, n_detected, event_recall, n_false_alarm_episodes, and false_alarms_per_30d. The table is the event-level operating characteristic on which select_threshold fits the decision threshold; the stages persist it as threshold_sweep.csv.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.threshold_sweep"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.time_row-Tuple{RunGeometry, Dates.DateTime}","page":"API reference","text":"time_row(geometry, t) -> Int\n\nPayload row whose mission time is t, the inverse of row_time rounded to the nearest row. Rows are 1-based and a time before start_sim_time yields a row below 1, which callers must reject rather than clamp: it means the batch does not belong to the payload the run was started from.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.time_row"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.top_legend!","page":"API reference","text":"top_legend!(figure, axis; nbanks = 1)\n\nHorizontal legend of the labelled series of axis above the axes, in the first row of the figure layout, in nbanks rows. Requires CairoMakie.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.top_legend!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.welch_psd-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"welch_psd(x, fs; segment_length, overlap = 0.5, taper = :hann, average = :median)\n    -> (freqs, psd)\nwelch_psd(records, fs; segment_length, overlap = 0.5, taper = :hann, average = :median)\n    -> (freqs, psd)\n\nOne-sided PSD estimate [Hz⁻¹] of the record x sampled at fs [Hz] from tapered periodograms (tapered_periodogram) of segments of segment_length samples overlapping by the fraction overlap. average is :mean (Welch) or :median (robust to transients; the median of the exponentially distributed periodogram is corrected by 1ln 2). The DC bin is dropped, so freqs starts at f_s  textttsegment_length.\n\nGiven a vector of records — the delivered runs of a record with holes — the segments of every record long enough to hold one are pooled into a single estimate, so that no segment spans a hole; a record shorter than a segment is skipped, and ArgumentError is thrown when none holds one.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.welch_psd"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.whiten_record-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"whiten_record(x, fs; psd) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nFrequency-domain whitening of the whole record x sampled at fs [Hz] by the one-sided noise PSD psd(f): X_k to X_k sqrt2  (f_s S_n(f_k)) with the DC bin zeroed, so that noise following psd becomes white with unit variance (one-sided PSD 2f_s). Applied once per record, before windowing: the tapered periodogram of a window of the white series is unbiased irrespective of the PSD slope (tapered_periodogram), whereas the periodogram of a separately whitened window is the PSD smoothed by the taper's main lobe. The filter is circular; on real records the first and last windows are edge-affected.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.whiten_record"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.whitening_psd!-Tuple{ReplayState, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"API reference","text":"whitening_psd!(state, window) -> (psd, psd_row)\n\nWhitening PSD of window in a replay: the detector's static PSD with psd_row = 0, or, under TrailingWelch, the causal PSD estimate over the delivered record behind the window's conditioning stretch and the last row it was made on — reused while that end has moved by less than refresh_rows, redone otherwise, and replaced by the static PSD while fewer than one segment of rows is on the ground.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.whitening_psd!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_count-Tuple{Integer, Integer, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"window_count(n_points, window_size, step_size) -> Int\n\nNumber of sliding windows of window_size samples advancing by step_size over a record of n_points samples; throws when the record is shorter than one window or the geometry is invalid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_count"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_features-Tuple{AbstractVecOrMat{<:Real}, Real}","page":"API reference","text":"window_features(A, fs; window_size, step_size, low_band, high_band,\n                band_edges = [1e-3, 5e-3, 1e-1], feature_set,\n                combination = :mean) -> Matrix{Float32}\n\nFeature matrix of the sliding windows of the (whitened) record A sampled at fs [Hz]: one row per window of window_size samples advancing by step_size, the columns named by feature_names and computed by extract_features with the analysis bands low_band, high_band [Hz] (:whitened) or the band_edges [Hz] (:bands). A matrix A holds several synchronous channels, one per column, each whitened by its own PSD, combined as combination says (CHANNEL_COMBINATIONS).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_features"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_indices-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"window_indices(features_path) -> Vector{Int}\n\nRecord window index of every row of a feature table, from its sidecar <stem>.toml: first_window, first_window + 1, … over n_windows rows for the product of a record without gaps, and the windows of every stretch in turn (stretches, a list of tables with first_window and n_windows) for the product of a record with gaps, where the index jumps between stretches. ArgumentError without a sidecar, without n_windows, or for stretches that are not in ascending order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_indices"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_labels-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}, AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API reference","text":"window_labels(raw_labels, raw_snrs; window_size, step_size) -> (labels, snrs)\n\nPer-window labels of the point-wise raw_labels and signal-to-noise ratios raw_snrs under the sliding-window geometry of window_features: a window is positive (label 1) when any of its samples is labelled 1, and carries the largest per-sample SNR inside it. Returns labels::Vector{Int} and snrs::Vector{Float32}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_lost-Tuple{ReplayState, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"window_lost(state, m) -> Bool\n\nWhether window m can never become evaluable: its own rows, or more of its conditioning stretch than the scheduler's min_coverage admits, lie in the permanent holes of lost or pruned batches.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_lost"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_rows-Tuple{WindowScheduler, Integer}","page":"API reference","text":"window_rows(scheduler, m) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nPayload rows of window m.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_rows"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#StreamingInference.window_score","page":"API reference","text":"window_score(scorer, window, sample_rate) -> Float32\n\nScore of one conditioned window (samples at sample_rate [Hz]): a vector, or in a replay of several synchronous channels a matrix with one column per channel. Implemented by every concrete AbstractWindowScorer; the fallbacks throw an ArgumentError naming the scorer type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.window_score"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.windows_table-Tuple{ReplayState}","page":"API reference","text":"windows_table(state) -> DataFrame\n\nThe scored windows of a replay as a table, one row per WindowRecord, in the order they were scored; the column release_at is added for a Stateful scorer, whose windows are scored in content order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.windows_table"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.windows_touching-Tuple{WindowScheduler, AbstractUnitRange{<:Integer}}","page":"API reference","text":"windows_touching(scheduler, rows) -> UnitRange{Int}\n\nIndices of the windows that intersect rows.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.windows_touching"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.with_pipeline_root-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"with_pipeline_root(f, root)\n\nRun f() with root as the pipeline root (project_root) of every path resolved inside it, in this task and the tasks it spawns. Scripts run their stage inside it, with the root of their configuration (config_root).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.with_pipeline_root"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.write_csv-Tuple{AbstractString, Any}","page":"API reference","text":"write_csv(path, table; safe = true)\n\nWrite table with CSV.write at path, backing up an existing file first when safe. Returns path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.write_csv"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#StreamingInference.write_toml-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractDict}","page":"API reference","text":"write_toml(path, data; safe = true, tag = true)\n\nWrite the dictionary data as TOML at path, backing up an existing file first (backup_existing!) when safe, and merging the provenance sections when tag. Returns path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"StreamingInference.write_toml"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Streaming-replay","page":"Streaming replay","text":"","title":"Streaming replay"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Run-interface","page":"Streaming replay","text":"A run is anything that implements the interface of AbstractTelemetryRun: its geometry (run_geometry: sampling rate, segment length, segments per batch, samples per batch, epoch, producer version), its batches (list_batches: delivered, lost or pruned, each with the payload rows it covers), the samples of a delivered batch (read_batch), the arrival feed in time order (arrival_events), and the lifecycle state (run_state). MemoryTelemetryRun holds a whole record in memory; an adapter over a producer's run directory implements the same five functions.","title":"Run interface"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Scheduling-and-conditioning","page":"Streaming replay","text":"Replaying the feed (replay_run) maintains the delivered rows as a set of disjoint intervals (Coverage), so the order of arrivals does not matter. A lost or pruned batch is a permanent hole, which later arrivals never fill.\n\nA window is scored once, at the time of the arrival that completes its conditioning stretch: its own rows widened by context_windows window lengths on each side and cut to the record. The stretch must be delivered to at least min_coverage, and the window's own rows entirely, so a hole inside a window is never scored across (WindowScheduler, conditioning_rows). The delivered stretch is high-passed and, when the detector has a PSD, whitened as a whole, and the window is cut from it (condition_window). The first windows of a record, and any isolated window, are scored on shorter context and are affected by the record edges.","title":"Scheduling and conditioning"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Estimators-and-ordered-release","page":"Streaming replay","text":"The detector owns the conditioning; the method applied to each conditioned window is an estimator (AbstractWindowEstimator). A detector needs a scalar one (AbstractWindowScorer, implementing window_score).\n\nAn estimator declares its memory (estimator_memory). A Stateless one is scored as each window completes, in arrival order, which after an outage or a retransmission is not content order. A Stateful one (a reservoir, a sequential posterior) must see the windows in content order, each once, with every hole declared. For it the replay conditions each window when it completes, holds it, and releases the held windows by increasing index (OrderedCommit). A run of windows that can never be scored, because a lost batch lies in its own rows or in more of its stretch than min_coverage admits, is declared by one GapEvent (cause :lost) passed to the estimator (estimator_gap!) before the window after it. A missing window holds back every later one; at the end of the feed the missing windows are declared :undelivered, and an order_horizon bounds the wait during a replay (:horizon), after which a window that completes is late and is skipped and counted, or refused (late_policy). Every scored row then records release_at beside complete_at, and alerts are timed by it (scored_at). replay_state returns the finalised replay, from which windows_table and gaps_table are read.","title":"Estimators and ordered release"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Causal-whitening","page":"Streaming replay","text":"With trailing_psd set to a TrailingWelch, every window is whitened by a Welch estimate of the delivered record behind it instead of a fixed PSD: nothing that has not reached the ground enters the estimate. The segments of all delivered runs in the trailing span are pooled, so no segment crosses a hole, and the estimate is refreshed as the record grows.","title":"Causal whitening"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Thresholds-and-alerts","page":"Streaming replay","text":"select_threshold fixes the decision threshold on a calibration block, by a target rate of false-alarm episodes (\"far\"), a window false-positive rate (\"fpr\") or Youden's index (\"youden\"), and threshold_sweep tabulates the operating characteristic. alert_latency_table turns the windows of a replay into alerts: an alert is a run of persistence consecutive alarmed windows, raised by the arrival that completes it; it is credited to an event when it overlaps the event's credited span, and every other alert counts as a false-alarm episode.","title":"Thresholds and alerts"},{"category":"section","location":"replay/#Pipeline-root-and-provenance","page":"Streaming replay","text":"Relative paths of a configuration resolve against the pipeline root (project_root): the root set by with_pipeline_root, the environment variable STREAMINGINFERENCE_ROOT, or the nearest directory above the active environment whose Project.toml declares a package. config_root derives the root from the location of a configuration file. Run provenance records the git state of that root, the packages of the pipeline with their revisions (layer_provenance), the hardware and the resolved environment (provenance); data products are identified by SHA-256 digests of their parameters and inputs (parameter_digest, content_digest, product_table).","title":"Pipeline root and provenance"},{"category":"section","location":"#StreamingInference.jl","page":"Home","text":"Windowed analysis of a time series that is delivered in batches: late, out of order, and with permanent holes. The package keeps track of which part of the record is on the ground, schedules each window once the stretch around it has arrived, conditions it (high-pass, whitening by a static or a causal PSD estimate), and passes it to an estimator. Evaluation acts on what the estimator returns: thresholds chosen on a calibration block, event-level metrics, false-alarm rates and alert latencies.\n\nThe estimator is supplied by the user. Nothing in the package depends on a physical domain or on a particular method; a detector score, a parameter estimate or a forecast plug into the same chain.","title":"StreamingInference.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Layout-of-the-package","page":"Home","text":"Part Contents\nEstimators AbstractWindowEstimator, the scalar AbstractWindowScorer with window_score, score_label, score_bounds; the memory trait estimator_memory (Stateless, Stateful); GapEvent, estimator_gap!, reset_estimator!; the spectral FeatureMap of a conditioned window\nStreaming replay the run interface (AbstractTelemetryRun, MemoryTelemetryRun), Coverage, WindowScheduler, StreamingDetector, condition_window, TrailingWelch, replay_run, follow_run, replay_state, windows_table, gaps_table, alert_latency_table\nSignal processing synthesize_noise, tapered_periodogram, network_periodogram, welch_psd, smooth_psd, interpolated_psd, highpass_record, whiten_record, matched_filter_snr, scale_to_snr, place_signal!\nFeatures and labels extract_features, window_features, window_labels, finite_stretches, window_indices, fixed_spans, span_labels, chronological_split\nEvaluation roc_curve, roc_auc, contiguous_runs, event_metrics, threshold_sweep, select_threshold\nConfiguration and provenance load_config, cfgget, section, with_pipeline_root, config_root, project_root, resolvepath, provenance, git_provenance, layer_provenance, hardware_fingerprint, parameter_digest, content_digest, product_table, recorded_channels\nFigures (CairoMakie extension) figure_theme, save_figure, figure_roc, figure_threshold_sweep, figure_sensitivity, figure_score_distribution, figure_telemetry_alerts, animate_mission_replay","title":"Layout of the package"},{"category":"section","location":"#Example","page":"Home","text":"A replay of an in-memory run through a scorer that returns the RMS of the whitened window:\n\nusing StreamingInference, Dates, Random\n\nstruct RMSScorer <: AbstractWindowScorer end\nStreamingInference.window_score(::RMSScorer, w::AbstractVector{<:Real}, ::Real) =\n    Float32(sqrt(sum(abs2, w) / length(w)))\n\nfs = 0.2                                     # sampling rate [Hz]\npsd(f) = 1e-40 * (1 + (1e-3 / f)^2)          # one-sided noise PSD [1/Hz]\npayload = synthesize_noise(Xoshiro(3), 8000, fs; psd = psd, f_min = 1e-5)\n\n# 80 batches of 10 segments of 50 s, one delivered every 10 minutes\ngeometry = RunGeometry(fs, 50.0, 10, DateTime(2035), \"example\")\nevents = [ArrivalEvent(DateTime(2035) + Second(600k), \"LIVE_batch_$k\", :ingested, 0) for k in 1:80]\nrun = MemoryTelemetryRun(geometry, payload, events)\n\ndetector = StreamingDetector(RMSScorer(), 1.5; sample_rate = fs, window_size = 1000,\n                             step_size = 100, psd = psd, context_windows = 1)\nwindows = replay_run(run, detector)\n\nStreaming replay describes the time model behind replay_run; the API reference lists every name.","title":"Example"}]
}
